        "subject": "LU-20611 lfs: name the unrecognized find option",
        "message": "LU-20611 lfs: name the unrecognized find option\n\nlfs find printed argv[optind - 1] for an unknown option.  When the\nbad character is inside a word, such as 'x' in -lxy, getopt has\nnot moved optind past that word, so the message named the word\nbefore it, often the search path.  Print the word getopt was in.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 905b7685c1cc (\"LU-930 utils: add --help option to lfs sub-commands\")\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ie141cfa961b48005e11aee8c9429dbc6a2452eac\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70745\nReviewed-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Chakshu Kansal <ckansal@ddn.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
